SUMMARY
======================================================================
Over the next 12 months, the forecast shows that the highest monthly activity will come from remote code execution vulnerabilities, with about 2,016 new CVEs per month, followed closely by miscellaneous vulnerabilities at roughly 1,984 per month, and denial of service at around 600 per month. The fastest-growing threats are remote code execution, which rises from about 365 to 2,016 CVEs per month, miscellaneous vulnerabilities from about 1,204 to 1,984, and cross-site scripting from about 78 to 533. The total projected economic loss over the full 12-month period is approximately $404 million on average, with a median and a very tight 90% range all at $404,643,266, indicating extremely high confidence in the loss estimate. The sectors facing the most loss exposure are Professional Services, with a mean loss of about $119.5 million, Manufacturing at about $100.3 million, and Finance at about $76.6 million. The value-at-risk figures for these sectors are nearly identical to their means, reinforcing the narrow range of outcomes.

